---
title: "Duolingo"
description: "Duolingo lesson history — French and Turkish early on, an ongoing Greek streak since April 2026."
date: 2026-08-02
---

{% set habit = "duolingo" | getHabit %}

<p><a href="{{ '/habits/' | url }}">← All habits</a></p>

{% if habit %}
<p>{{ habit.description }} Source: {{ habit.source }}.</p>

<p><a href="https://www.duolingo.com/profile/SiJobling?via=share_profile_qr">Join me on Duolingo</a> or follow me with the QR code below.</p>

<p><a href="https://www.duolingo.com/profile/SiJobling?via=share_profile_qr"><img alt="QR code to follow Si Jobling on Duolingo" src="/assets/images/Duolingo_Sharing-782x1024.png"></a></p>

{% set lastLevel = lastKnownValue(habit.entries, 'level') %}
<div class="habit-stats">
  <div class="habit-stat">
    <span class="habit-stat__label">Sessions logged</span>
    <span class="habit-stat__value">{{ habit.sessionCount }}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="habit-stat">
    <span class="habit-stat__label">Current language</span>
    <span class="habit-stat__value">{{ habit.latest.language }}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="habit-stat">
    <span class="habit-stat__label">Total time practiced</span>
    <span class="habit-stat__value">{{ habit.stats.primaryTotal | formatMetric(habit.primaryMetric) }}</span>
  </div>
  {% for stat in habit.stats.extra %}
    <div class="habit-stat">
      <span class="habit-stat__label">{{ stat.label }}</span>
      <span class="habit-stat__value">{{ stat.value | formatMetric(stat) }}</span>
    </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="habit-stat">
    <span class="habit-stat__label">Best combo</span>
    <span class="habit-stat__value">{{ habit.stats.secondaryBest | formatMetric(habit.secondaryMetric) }}</span>
  </div>
  {% if lastLevel %}
    <div class="habit-stat">
      <span class="habit-stat__label">Last recorded level</span>
      <span class="habit-stat__value">{{ lastLevel.level }} <small>({{ lastLevel.language }}, {{ lastLevel.date | readableIsoDate }})</small></span>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<p><em>The export only tags a language and level on some rows — French and Turkish are labelled throughout, but the Greek streak stops recording a level after {{ lastLevel.date | readableIsoDate }} even though it's been going ever since. Treat "last recorded level" as a floor, not the current level. XP isn't shown here either — the source scan regularly confuses it with the phone's battery level, so it's not trustworthy.</em></p>

<h2>Monthly totals</h2>
<p>The full lesson-by-lesson log is too long to list on one page, so it's merged by day and broken out by month below - each month links through to its day-by-day breakdown.</p>
<div class="habit-table-wrap">
  <table class="habit-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Month</th>
        <th scope="col">Total duration</th>
        <th scope="col">Accuracy (range)</th>
        <th scope="col">Accuracy (avg)</th>
        <th scope="col">Highest combo</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for month in duolingoMonths | reverse %}
        <tr>
          <td><a href="{{ month.url | url }}">{{ month.label }}</a></td>
          <td>{{ month.totals.totalDurationSeconds | formatDuration }}</td>
          <td>{% if month.totals.accuracyMin != null %}{{ month.totals.accuracyMin }}–{{ month.totals.accuracyMax }}%{% else %}-{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{% if month.totals.accuracyAvg != null %}{{ month.totals.accuracyAvg }}%{% else %}-{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ month.totals.bestCombo or "-" }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{% else %}
<p>No data yet.</p>
{% endif %}
